  "text": "proprium.commemoratio-omnium-fidelium-defunctorum-missa-i-offertorium",
  "about": "The offertorium of the formulary “Commemoration of All the Faithful Departed — Mass I” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "Lord Jesus Christ, King of glory, set free the souls of all the faithful departed from the punishments of hell and from the deep pit; set them free from the mouth of the lion, that the abyss may not swallow them up, that they may not fall into darkness; but may the holy standard-bearer Michael bring them into the holy light: Which You promised long ago to Abraham and to his seed. Sacrificial gifts and prayers of praise we offer to You, O Lord: do You receive them on behalf of those souls whom we commemorate today; make them, O Lord, pass over from death to life. Which You promised long ago to Abraham and to his seed.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w061", "w062"], "anchor": "w062", "gloss": "we commemorate" }] }
  },
